## Backtest Period Split

- Development period: 2012-01-01 to 2021-12-31 (10 years)
- Out-of-sample test period: 2022-01-01 to 2024-12-31 (3 years)
- Chosen because: development period captures multiple regimes (2008 financial crash, 2018 selloff,
  2020 COVID crash); out-of-sample period includes the 2022 rate-hiking
  selloff, giving it a genuine stress test rather than only calm markets
- Commitment: strategy parameters will not be modified based on
  out-of-sample results. Any future change requires a new strategy version
  (v1.1+) applied prospectively, not retroactively to this test.


## Out-of-sample evaluation criteria (written [10/10/2026], BEFORE running)

Test period: 2022-01-01 to 2026-6-31 (as committed in spec)

I will consider v1.0 to have "held up" if:
- Out-of-sample Sharpe is positive and within the range of my development
  sub-period Sharpes (min to max, from Week 6 Day 4)
- Max drawdown is not dramatically worse than the benchmark's over the same period
- Results are directionally consistent with development (positive information ratio)

I will consider it to have "not held up" if Sharpe is negative or drawdown
is far beyond anything seen in development.

Either way, I will NOT modify v1.0 parameters in response. Any change = new
version (v1.1+), applied going forward only, with the reasoning documented.
